# @autopoietic — the prism class permitted to fold back. A prism that
# imports `in @autopoietic` declares the bilateral commitment (per
# recognition #37's Pask-agreement reading of `requires`) that its
# operations consume its own prior crystals as input. The substrate's
# self-production discipline at the prism-class altitude.
#
# Homage: Humberto Maturana (1928–2021) + Francisco Varela (1946–
# 2001); 1972 (*De máquinas y seres vivos*, Editorial Universitaria)
# 1980 (*Autopoiesis and Cognition*, D. Reidel). The biological-
# epistemological tradition that named the operational form: a
# system is autopoietic iff the network of productions produces the
# conditions for its own continued production. The structure is
# circular; the boundary is self-maintained; the system is
# operationally closed while structurally open.
#
# === The recognition (#104 chain P2, 2026-06-29) ===
#
# This shard is the second tier of the @bauchladen ← @autopoietic ←
# @fate dependency chain per canonical spec at `docs/specs/
# bauchladen-autopoietic-fate.md` (Mara `4575340`, ~2727 lines). The
# first tier (@bauchladen) landed at `66e1ab8` as the prism-altitude
# content-addressing discipline (Schmidt homage; the typed display
# the substrate browses). This shard names the SECOND tier: the
# prism class permitted to fold the tray's contents back as its own
# input.
#
# Witnesses for the chain's #104 candidacy:
#   - Canonical spec at `docs/specs/bauchladen-autopoietic-fate.md`
#     §3 (the @autopoietic prism-class shape this shard discharges).
#   - The first-tier landing at `shards/bauchladen.mirror`
#     (`66e1ab8`); the dependency this shard structurally rests on.
#   - The forward-promised third tier at `shards/fate.mirror` (per
#     spec §4); @fate is `in @autopoietic` is `in @bauchladen`.
#   - The 28KB grammar-class precursor at `docs/specs/autopoietic-
#     grammar-spec.md` (Reed 2026-06-04); the substrate had the word
#     at the precursor altitude; this shard is the LIFT to prism
#     class (per spec §3.6), not the original naming.
#   - The 750+-line cybernetic-species shard at `shards/
#     epistemologic/cybernetic/autopoiesis.mirror` (#379, Maturana-
#     Varela 1980 + Soto-Andrade & Varela 1984 bridge, ρ = adjoint);
#     the property altitude this prism class lifts.
#   - Taut scout `27c8592` (grep-verifies zero substrate-decl hits
#     for `@autopoietic` at prism altitude AND that the 28KB
#     grammar-spec is the unique precursor; the lift framing is
#     substrate-pull-confirmed, not asserted).
#
# === Why @bauchladen is structurally necessary: the Lawvere fixed-
#     point condition is MATHEMATICAL, not stylistic ===
#
# Per spec §3.2's structural argument: fold-back requires STABLE
# IDENTITY for prior outputs to address. A system that consumes its
# own prior outputs must NAME them unambiguously — "I am consuming
# the X I produced at tick N, not some Y that happens to resemble X."
#
# Without content-addressing, the naming is unstable. The Lawvere
# fixed-point condition (per `@epistemologic/math/lawvere` +
# Soto-Andrade & Varela 1984) requires that the prism's tick-to-tick
# map admit a fixed point — an OID f such that `hash(P(f)) == f`.
# The substrate's content-addressing exhibits this AT CONSTRUCTION
# TIME: the OID is the hash; the equality check is byte-equality on
# the OID layer.
#
# Without @bauchladen, the equality check is not well-defined; the
# fixed-point condition is unverifiable; "fold-back" reduces to
# mere recurrence with ambiguous reference, which is NOT autopoiesis
# in Maturana-Varela's sense (per spec §3.2 final paragraph). The
# dependency is mathematical: stable identity is a load-bearing
# precondition for the operational closure condition Maturana-Varela
# 1980 names as the definition of autopoiesis.
#
# This is why `in @bauchladen` is the first declaration in the
# import block above. The order is not stylistic; the chain
# `@bauchladen ← @autopoietic` reflects a structural prerequisite
# the Lawvere fixed-point machinery requires.
#
# === The 28KB grammar-class precursor: LIFT, not re-declaration ===
#
# Per spec §3.6: the @autopoietic prism-class declared here is the
# LIFT of a 28KB precursor at `docs/specs/autopoietic-grammar-
# spec.md` (Reed, 2026-06-04). The precursor declared `abstract
# grammar @autopoietic` with `boundary = @me | @reality` and
# `< @autopoietic` inheritance from `@actor` and `@runtime` — the
# pre-prism-keyword form, before [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-
# everything]] collapsed `grammar` / `trait` / `interface` / `type`
# to `prism`.
#
# The lift is MECHANICAL in form (`abstract grammar @autopoietic`
# → `prism @autopoietic`) and STRUCTURAL in placement (the
# `@bauchladen ← @autopoietic ← @fate` chain situates the lifted
# prism class between the content-addressing discipline below and
# the constrained-inference operator above).
#
# The inheritance discipline (spec §3.6, items 1-4):
#
#   1. This shard does NOT duplicate the precursor's content. The
#      28KB spec carries the OBC/ADO mappings, the extraction
#      analysis, the silence/fear/glue-work translations, the
#      MirrorStore-as-substrate argument; these stay in the spec.
#   2. The shard cross-references the precursor at the spec layer
#      (this docblock), not by re-declaration.
#   3. The precursor's boundary / inheritance / coupling vocabulary
#      remains the source-of-truth at the grammar altitude.
#   4. The 28KB spec is NOT obsolete; it is the substrate's history
#      of how the discipline came to be nameable at the prism
#      altitude. It stays in `docs/specs/` as the precursor reference.
#
# Substrate-already-had-the-word at the precursor altitude (per
# [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]); the substrate had
# `@autopoietic` at the grammar-class altitude for 25 days before
# this shard. The shard's contribution is the chain placement and
# the substrate-decl shape, not the discipline itself.
#
# === The #379 cybernetic property operationalized via Bauchladen ===
#
# `@epistemologic/cybernetic/autopoiesis` (per `shards/epistemologic/
# cybernetic/autopoiesis.mirror`, 750+ lines, landed 2026-06-09) is
# the SPECIES declaration at the cybernetic-ancestor altitude. It
# carries typed carriers (organization, component, autopoietic_
# system), the predicate `autopoietic_closure_holds(s)`, and the τ-
# actions (produce, couple, close, gauge_act) for the four held
# readings (A self-production, B structural coupling, C operational
# closure, E bundle structure group). ρ = adjoint representation.
#
# This shard LIFTS that property to a prism class. The lift's
# structural form (per spec §3.1):
#
#   Altitude                                           Carrier shape
#   ----------------------------------                 -------------
#   @epistemologic/property/autopoietic                predicate
#     (verifier: `autopoietic(type)`)
#   @epistemologic/cybernetic/autopoiesis              typed carriers
#     (species: lock_pair instantiation; ρ=adjoint)    + predicate
#   @autopoietic (THIS SHARD)                          prism contract
#     (prism class: commitment to fold-back)
#
# The three altitudes STACK; they do NOT compete. The property
# declares verifiability; the species declares the cybernetic-
# ancestor placement; the prism class declares the commitment to
# produce verifiable output. Per spec §3.4, Maturana-Varela's
# operational form is operationalized at the substrate altitude via
# content-addressed-crystal accumulation in the Bauchladen tray:
#
#   Maturana-Varela                Substrate
#   --------------------------     -------------------------------
#   Network of productions         Set of @autopoietic prisms
#                                  operating over the Bauchladen tray
#   Components produced            Crystals added to the tray
#   Conditions for continued       Prior crystals consulted as inputs
#     production                   to future inferences
#   Boundary (membrane)            Crystals nameable by OID
#   Structural coupling            @fate inferences reading external
#                                  @io data and emitting crystals
#   Operational closure            The tray-operation set closes —
#                                  every product (crystal) is the
#                                  input to some operation
#
# The Lawvere fixed-point witness (Soto-Andrade & Varela 1984): at
# some tick a @fate inference will emit a crystal whose OID equals
# an OID it consulted as input. The substrate exhibits this
# constructively — content-addressing makes the OID equality check
# trivial.
#
# === The candidates(hole) migration home (per spec §4.7) ===
#
# The boot-floor file `boot/std/fate/tournament.mirror` declared
# `candidates(hole) -> [resolution]` with a five-ganglion body
# (`@ai/abyss.depth`, `@ai/introject.pattern`, `@ai/cartographer.
# map`, `@ai/explorer.expand`, `@ai/fate.select`). The boot/
# directory was killed in spring-clean. The action's content was
# orphaned: 15+ specs still reference it (kintsugi-tournament.md,
# substrate-native-fate-tournament.md, kintsugi-wiring.md, code-
# metalogue-surface.md, lsp-and-mcp.md, road-to-1.0.md, gap-tension-
# tensor-substrate.md, ants-colonies-stigmergy.md, others), but no
# shard in `shards/` carries the action declaration.
#
# Taut scout `27c8592` §1 / §2.4 surfaced this as the most
# operationally significant unresolved tension. Spec §4.7's
# four-row migration mapping table identifies @autopoietic's tick-
# action carrier as the migration home:
#
#   Boot-floor element                          Chain landing site
#   -----------------------------------------   -----------------------
#   `candidates(hole) -> [resolution]`          @autopoietic's `tick`
#     (the action)                              action; @fate inherits
#                                               via `in @autopoietic`
#   The five-ganglion body (depth, pattern,    The autopoietic-tick's
#     map, expand, select)                      components; per spec
#                                               §3.4 the components
#                                               are the autopoietic-
#                                               system's `produce`
#                                               operations
#   `[resolution]` (the return type)           Content-addressed
#                                               crystals in the
#                                               @bauchladen tray
#   The five-ganglion optical-source           The OPERATIONAL
#     shards (already in `shards/optics/        realization of the
#     source/ganglion/*.mirror` per             autopoietic-tick's
#     recognition #58)                          components
#
# The migration is NOT a re-write; it is a re-anchoring. The boot/
# content was spring-cleaned because it had no substrate-decl host;
# this shard provides the host. The `tick` action declared below
# inherits the `candidates(hole)`-shape semantics under the
# autopoietic discipline.
#
# === Forward-promised inheritors (per spec §3.5) ===
#
# Prisms that will import `in @autopoietic` once the chain lands:
#
#   - @fate (this chain's third tier; per spec §4): Fate inferences
#     consult prior crystals and emit new crystals; the fold-back
#     IS Fate's learning mechanism.
#   - @glue (forward-promised): @glue uses @fate to pick which
#     morphism to apply; @glue is autopoietic via @fate.
#   - @kintsugi (forward-promised): @kintsugi drives the D-flow's
#     per-step decisions via @fate; the kintsugi loop IS autopoietic.
#   - @reflection (forward-promised): per [[architecture-reflection-
#     thinks-in-spectral-questions]], Reflection consults the
#     pipeline's spectral-altitude history and emits altitude-
#     selection crystals; Reflection IS autopoietic.
#   - @spectral/metalogue (forward-promised; the metalogue's turn
#     chain consults prior turns via `in_reply_to`; the metalogue
#     session IS autopoietic).
#
# Asymmetry: NOT every prism becomes @autopoietic. Many prisms are
# stateless inference functions (e.g., @code/metalogue shims that
# translate substrate declarations to language-specific AST nodes).
# Such prisms import `in @bauchladen` (outputs are content-addressed
# crystals) but do NOT import `in @autopoietic` (they do not fold
# their outputs back as inputs). The asymmetry is structural and
# healthy.
#
# === No operational sibling THIS tick ===
#
# Per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] no `@mirror/cybernetics/
# autopoietic` operational sibling lands at this tick. The substrate
# ALREADY has the operational machinery (content-addressed OID layer
# at @mirror/store; the autopoiesis property at @epistemologic/
# cybernetic/autopoiesis with four held readings; gen_prism's
# typed-actor autopoietic instance; the librarian altitude at
# @spectral/db as the autopoietic memory layer). This shard names
# the prism-class contract so downstream shards can declare
# `requires autopoietic_closure_holds(my_prism)` and `requires
# lawvere_fixed_point(my_prism)` rather than re-state the obligations
# per species. The deeper sub-shards (`shards/autopoietic/fold.
# mirror` with `fold_back` + `exhibit_fixed_point` per spec §3.3)
# follow when consumers pull.
#
